<div class="hb-prose">
  <p>The <?php echo $hb->nav('Icon Manager', 'icons'); ?> manages the website's symbols, for example for cards or lists. When you choose an icon in a block, it comes from this collection. Each icon shows whether it's part of nibbly's standard set or was added later.</p>
</div>
<?php echo $hb->shot('icons.webp', 'Icon Manager with search field, sorting, global stroke width and a grid of icons', '<b>Icon Manager.</b> Search, sorting and global stroke width at the top, all icons below.'); ?>
<dl class="hb-fields">
  <div><dt>Combine events</dt><dd>Choose <b>Playback → Combine events</b> to set what happens on appearance, hover, pointer exit and click. From and To select a percentage range of the original animation for each event. With a click toggle, the first click moves to the active pose and the second returns to the inactive pose. A hover loop ends on exit or click. In the page editor you can override individual events for one placement.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Category and library</dt><dd>The category describes how you use an icon. Choose an existing category or type a new name. The library identifies its origin. nibbly fills this in for useAnimations and Iconify imports. Use the links above the list to combine category, library and animation filters with your search. An icon with playback set to Static counts as static.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Animated icons</dt><dd>Search for <b>useAnimations</b>. The label below each icon tells you how to try its preview. Move away from Mail during playback to reverse it. Send and Refresh replay on each click. Click a toggle twice to see both states. Under <b>Edit → Playback</b> you can restore the original interaction, select a different trigger or reverse the direction. This is the default for new and existing placements. With reduced motion, states change instantly.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Playback per placement</dt><dd>Open the card or icon in the page editor. For a Lottie icon, you can choose the interaction and playback direction for this placement and try them on the preview icon. Choose “Library default” to inherit that setting again.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Import from icon library</dt><dd>Searches a large, free icon collection. Icons you pick are stored on your own website; the icon set's licence is shown. Imported icons use the global stroke width; their style and licence source are kept when you save.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Add icon</dt><dd>For your own icons: enter a unique key, a label and the SVG code. The preview shows right away how it looks. <?php echo $hb->ui('Use currentColor'); ?> makes the icon take on the website's text colour.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Style</dt><dd>In the edit form you set whether an icon is drawn as “Line (outline)” or “Solid (filled)”. nibbly detects this from the SVG code when you paste it and suggests the matching value; change it if needed.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Stroke width (global)</dt><dd>The field in the bar at the top sets the line weight for all line icons that don't have their own. The default is 2. This keeps icons from different collections looking consistent.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Stroke width per icon</dt><dd>With <b>Global</b> on, the icon uses the global stroke width. The number field shows its current value. Turn Global off to enter a width from 0.25 to 6 for this icon.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Editing and deleting</dt><dd>If an icon's key changes or it's deleted, content that uses it shows a default icon.</dd></div>
</dl>
